<title>AUSTRALIA: Wage restraint benefitting inflation,rates - Howard.</title>
<headline>Wage restraint benefitting inflation,rates - Howard.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Prime Minister John Howard said on Tuesday it was clear that wage restraint was contributing to lower inflation and lower interest rates.</p>
<p>&quot;He said it was clear that wage restraint was contributing to low inflation, leading to lower interest rates,&quot; a Coalition spokesman quoted Howard as telling government parliamentarians.</p>
<p>The spokesman said Howard had described last Friday's 0.5 percentage point reduction in official interest rates to 5.5 percent as a &quot;budget bonus&quot;.  </p>
<p>The Reserve Bank's decision to cut rates followed data the previous day showing first quarter average weekly earnings growth was revised down to a rise of 1.0 percent from 1.3 percent, giving an annual rise of 4.3 percent, down from 4.6 percent.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
